</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="russia_ukraine_war::commodity_supply_gap" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="ai_power_shift::model_capability_growth" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sanctions and attendant export controls on advanced semiconductors, cloud services and tooling increase hardware scarcity and compliance costs for liable suppliers, directly slowing the ability of teams (including global commercial labs) to train and iterate very large models.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="middle_east_maritime::tanker_transit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Tightened sanctions on Russian oil push buying demand toward Middle Eastern suppliers and increase spot cargo purchases and re-exports, elevating tanker traffic through key regional waterways.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_maritime</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="north_korea_escalation::arms_tech_proliferation" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Intensified sanctions on Russia drive Moscow to seek off‑market suppliers and barter partners (including North Korea), producing direct transfers and technical exchanges that increase the flow of arms and dual‑use know‑how to/from DPRK.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">north_korea_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="north_korea_escalation::logistics_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">As sanctions constrict conventional trade routes, Russian actors expand clandestine maritime and overland procurement networks with North Korean intermediaries, which builds DPRK's smuggling, transshipment and sustainment capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">north_korea_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="us_china_competition::regulatory_intervention" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Policymakers’ expanded use of sectoral and secondary sanctions against Russia creates institutional precedent and technical frameworks (e.g., export controls, finance screening) that are then adapted and applied to China-related trade and investment, increasing the frequency and severity of regulatory interventions.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_competition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="us_china_competition::foreign_investor_sent" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">The proliferation of sanctions and the risk of secondary penalties increase political and legal risk perceptions among global investors, reducing appetite for capital allocation to large geopolitical targets (including China) and lowering overall investor sentiment.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_competition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="concept::sanctions_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">instance_of</data>
</edge>
