<edge source="middle_east_maritime::oil_price_level" target="ai_power_shift::model_capability_growth" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Elevated global oil prices increase energy and operational costs for large-scale model training and inference (through higher power and transportation costs), reducing available compute budgets and slowing the rate of capability-improving experiments and large-scale training runs.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_maritime</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_maritime::oil_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::strike_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A prolonged increase in global oil prices driven by Middle East maritime risk increases export earnings and fiscal space for an oil-exporting belligerent, enabling higher procurement/sustainment of munitions and fuel and thereby supporting a higher tempo of kinetic strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_maritime</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="middle_east_maritime::oil_price_level" target="us_china_competition::corporate_relocation" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained spikes in global oil prices raise transportation and input costs for energy‑intensive and long‑supply‑chain manufacturers, incentivizing firms to shift production or sourcing away from more exposed jurisdictions (accelerating relocations).</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_maritime</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_competition</data>
</edge>
