<edge source="north_korea_escalation::arms_tech_proliferation" target="ai_power_shift::safety_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased flow of dual-use cyber and AI-related tools from or via actors linked to North Korean escalation enables state and non-state operators to deploy or weaponize AI systems more widely, increasing the frequency and severity of safety and security incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">north_korea_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="north_korea_escalation::arms_tech_proliferation" target="middle_east_maritime::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">An escalation in North Korea drives an uptick in outbound transfers of anti-ship missiles, cruise missile kits and guidance components to regional proxies and clients, materially raising those actors' capability and willingness to conduct attacks on ships and offshore infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">north_korea_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_maritime</data>
</edge>
<edge source="north_korea_escalation::arms_tech_proliferation" target="russia_ukraine_war::allied_military_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">North Korean escalation increases flows of missiles, rockets, artillery rounds and drones from DPRK-linked suppliers to Russia, directly raising the volume of external military materiel available to Russian forces.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">north_korea_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="north_korea_escalation::arms_tech_proliferation" target="russia_ukraine_war::strike_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Additional munitions and strike-capable systems supplied from North Korean sources augment Russian stocks and enable a higher tempo and scale of missile, artillery and UAV strikes in the theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">north_korea_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="north_korea_escalation::arms_tech_proliferation" target="us_china_competition::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid transfers or visible proliferation of North Korean missile/dual‑use tech to regional proxies prompt the US to escalate counterproliferation diplomacy and pressure China to police transfers, producing an observable rise in US–China strategic contestation.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">north_korea_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_competition</data>
</edge>
